who let them do this  how is this allowed  why are the subtitles one of the  strangest things in stranger things  in this video we're going to look at the  10 strangest things from netflix's hit  series stranger things and i don't mean  things like demogorgons or alternate  dimensions i mean things like the  subtitles  also stick around to the end for what  i'd say is the absolute strangest thing  from all four seasons of stranger things  [Music]  as i mentioned before the subtitles for  the series are absolutely bonkers  especially in season 4 of the show one  of netflix's employees on their  subtitling team carly webster explained  we have complete free reign as far as  i'm aware i don't think there was  anything that we were told we couldn't  add as far as production being involved  and telling us how far we can take it  that didn't happen they put a lot of  thought and effort into subtitling each  episode and the team did a great job of  explaining the show's sounds more  accurately than any other show i've seen  before they went to great lengths to  make sure anyone who is deaf or hard of  hearing would be able to enjoy the show  to the same extent as anyone else and  they were spot on with every line up  next is will's haircut it went from okay  to bad to worse to absolutely terrible  the actor who plays will buyers noah  schnapp apparently begged the show's  creators the duffer brothers to let him  have a different haircut for season 4  but they insisted that it was of the  times noah even joked that he plans on  making a powerpoint presentation as to  why he shouldn't have to have the bolt  cut in season 5 of the show so we'll  have to wait and see if its presentation  pans out like he wants  next up is the fact that in season 1  hopper turned 11 over to the authorities  and now they have such a close  relationship that it seems impossible he  would ever have been able to do such a  thing as part of an agreement he made  with the folks at hawkins laboratory  hopper agreed to give up 11's location  to save will although the kids were fine  in the end it's crazy to think he was  willing to give her up at one point and  now he would do anything to help her  even going so far as to break back into  a russian prison to fight a demogorgon  to potentially give her the upper hand  in fighting a greater threat in the  upside down definitely a complete 180 in  their relationship but we can't imagine  it any other way the next strangest  thing in the series takes place in  season 4 when will cries in the car  right next to mike and he doesn't seem  to notice at all i get that teenagers  can be oblivious but if someone is  sitting mere inches away from you  bawling their eyes out it should be  pretty easy to tell  i get that mike's thinking only about 11  in the moment but you'd think he'd speak  up and ask if will's okay i guess the  haircut must have distracted him too  much or something next up one of the  strangest things about the show lies in  the question of how a sci-fi 80s series  became one of the most popular tv shows  in entertainment history before stranger  things retro tv shows and sci-fi netflix  originals only appealed to a very small  audience but now stranger things has  become one of the most watched series of  all time on the platform and it's given  somewhat of a rebirth to 80s fashion  dungeons and dragons and even music from  the 80s for example kate bush's running  up that hill was a pretty popular song  in the 80s but since stranger things  season 4 was released spotify streams  for the song have gone up by over nine  thousand percent in the united states  and it's hit the top ten billboards for  both the us and the uk it's just crazy  that a sci-fi tv show about kids playing  dungeons and dragons could make such an  impact on the entertainment industry in  such a short period of time another  strange thing about the series is that  we're willing to sit through  movie-length episodes when typically  people hardly have the patience to sit  through a 20 minute sitcom while big  budget movie run times have seemingly  grown longer in recent years stranger  things lengthening of episodes is the  first popular instance of this happening  in the tv series medium i think it's  likely we'll begin to see other popular  shows release longer and longer episodes  as people become more willing to binge  for longer and longer especially on  shows with already well-established  casts and settings looking at you rings  of power next up is the fact that nancy  wheeler is pretty good with guns with  little to no guidance or training nancy  seems to be able to pick up almost any  firearm and use it perfectly she's  almost like a trained demogorgon  assassin capable of loading and firing  any gun she can get her hands on i  understand that she could have had some  sort of firearm training off-screen but  i think it's just so strange that they  went with her character for the  gunslinger either way it still works  really well the next strangest thing  about the series is from season one  again when the police found will's fake  body in the lake apparently the duffer  brothers thought a fake body would look  too well fake so they asked a 30 year  old woman to stand in or lie in for the  dummy body for several shots in the  first season we asked a stunt woman to  go into that icy 3am water as will  buyers so that it would look maximum  convincing said producer sean levy and i  have to say it did look pretty  convincing on the first watch the  runner-up for the strangest things in  stranger things is the fact that steve  harrington was supposed to die in season  one in the original story steve was  supposed to have died pretty early on  and jonathan's dad was supposed to be  the one who fought the demogorgon in the  end upon seeing joe kiri's acting in the  role though the duffer brothers decided  to rewrite the story and keep him around  seeing the show where it is now it's  almost impossible to imagine the gang  getting together without steve kiri has  done a fantastic job of playing the  mother henry over the younger actors and  he's also played a key role in the love  triangle with jonathan and nancy i mean  without him we wouldn't have this  [Laughter]  now the strangest thing of all in the  series has to be the fact that in every  season a new beloved character is always  killed off whether it be barbara in  season 1 bob in season 2 alexi in season  3 or chrissy and eddie in season 4 our  new favorite characters always seem to  die it's almost gotten to the point  where when we see a new character we  like each season we can almost guarantee  that they'll be dead by the end of it  very few new and likable characters have  made it past their debut season such as  dr owens and robin  this has to be one of the strangest  things about the show because it seems  all of these super likable characters  have their potential wasted in just a  matter of episodes honorable mentions  for new characters that died include max  who died but then came back to life kind  of like hopper jason and billy now this  is certainly not an all exhaustive list  of the strangest things in stranger  things so i'd like to see what you think  drop your favorite things from the  series in the comment section below also  maybe think about checking out the video  on your screen for some more of my  content don't forget to like and  subscribe and thanks for watching rocket  riley  you

